| notes         = Used to [[Kingly Deer|tame]] an {{Ilink|Kingly Deer}} [[Enraged White Deer]]. It has a 25%-33% chance to break when used. You may need 2-4+ to successfully tame an [[Enraged White Deer]].<br />
Although normal [[White Deer]] can't handle a human's weight, [[Enraged White Deer]] have extra strength that allows them to do so.

'''Failed''':<br />{{Sound|The white deer flees.}}

'''Failed''': <br />{{Sound|The white deer sniffs and wheezes, trying to withstand the taming.}}

'''Broke''': <br />{{Sound|Oh no... the enraged deer angrily ripped the fir cone from your hands!}}

'''Succeeded''': <br />{{Sound|You tamed the white deer.}}

'''Trying to tame a White Deer''':<br />{{Sound|You should try to enrage this deer before your taming attempt. That way you make sure it's strong enough to carry you.}}

'''Trying to tame a Desperate White Deer''':<br />{{Sound|This deer doesn't show enough strength and is too desperate already. Only enraged deer have the necessary power to carry you.}}


Take a [[Gold Ingot]] to [[Sweaty Cyclops]] and say: ''hi'', ''melt'', ''yes'', ''yes'' (you do not need to have completed [[The Sweaty Cyclops Quest]]). You will get a [[Cup of Molten Gold]]. Using it on a [[Fir Tree]] or a [[Fir Cone]] will give you a small chance (around 10%) to make a Golden Fir Cone.
